==Weaknesses==
<gallery type="slideshow">
SD1 (258).png|Ineffective Cryokinesis
TUH (172).png|Ineffective Intangibility
MoI (303).png|Intangible Opponents
SD1 (277).png|Psycholeopterran Predation
KBS (454).png|Fire Vulnerability
VoV2 (456).png|Electricity Vulnerability
SD1 (268).png|Hypnosis Vulnerability
</gallery>
Being a Necrofriggian, Big Chill is vulnerable to being hypnotized by a [[Psycholeopterran]]. His ice breath is also useless against Psycholeopterrans, as shown when [[Hypnotick]] escaped by using her own intangibility.<ref name="Malefactor">''[[Malefactor]]''</ref><ref name="SP1">''[[Showdown: Part 1]]''</ref>

Some objects are capable of touching Big Chill while he's intangible, those being: The Rustbucket II's netting,<ref name="KBS" /> the [[Shield of Seagle]],<ref name="VoVP2">''[[Vengeance of Vilgax: Part 2]]''</ref> the [[Techadon Factory]]'s defense systems,<ref>''[[Greetings From Techadon]]''</ref> and the [[Plumber Headquarters|Plumber Headquarters]]' prison cell door.<ref name="TUH" />

Big Chill's intangibility is useless against opponents who can also turn intangible, such as other Necrofriggians, as it will cancel out their ability to phase through them.<ref name="MoI" />

Although Big Chill is resistant to intense heat,<ref name="StLD" /> he can be harmed by fire.<ref name="KBS" />

Big Chill can be harmed by electricity, such as that generated by a [[Cerebrocrustacean]]<ref name="GCBC">''[[Good Copy, Bad Copy]]''</ref> and/or the Shield of Seagle.<ref name="VoVP2" />

Big Chill is vulnerable to intense sonic vibrations while intangible, such as those of an [[Ultimate Sonorosian]]'s [[Sonic Disc]]s, as demonstrated with several Necrofriggian guards on [[Mikd'lty]].<ref name="MoI" />

==History==
===Alien Force===
*Big Chill first appeared in ''[[Kevin's Big Score]]'', where he failed to stop [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]] from escaping in the [[Rustbucket II]] and later defeated [[Vulkanus]].
*In ''[[Max Out]]'', Big Chill battled some [[DNAlien]]s.
*In ''[[Plumbers' Helpers (Episode)|Plumbers' Helpers]]'', Big Chill put out a fire and saved [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] from falling to her death.
*In ''[[Alone Together]]'', Big Chill tried to cool down [[Reinrassig III]] and defeated a [[Dravec]] with his help.
*In ''[[Good Copy, Bad Copy]]'', Big Chill appeared thrice. Firstly, [[Albedo|Negative]] Big Chill fought some [[Forever Knights]] and was found by Gwen and Kevin. Later, Ben as Big Chill followed Gwen and Kevin and found them with [[Albedo]]. Lastly, Negative Big Chill battled [[Swampfire]] and was defeated by [[Brainstorm]], forcing him to switch into Negative [[Echo Echo]].
*In ''[[Save the Last Dance]]'', Big Chill was taken over by his reproduction instincts thrice. Whenever Ben attempted to turn into an alien other than Big Chill, the Omnitrix automatically and immediately turned him into Big Chill. Similarly, whenever the time called for it, Ben stopped doing whatever he is doing and transformed into Big Chill. He then started eating any metal object he could find and laid eggs and built a nest for them until the Omnitrix timed out, causing Ben to pass out, wake up in the middle of nowhere and forget everything he did. This kept happening until the eggs finally hatched, giving birth to Big Chill's Offspring.
**Footage of Big Chill from this episode was aired on TV in ''[[Fame]]''.
*In ''[[Birds of a Feather]]'', Big Chill froze a door to help [[Simian]] break it and encountered [[Lu]]. When Lu was thrown off the bridge by Simian, Big Chill switched into [[Jetray (Classic)|Jetray]] to save him.
*In ''[[Voided]]'', Big Chill defeated [[Dr. Animo (Classic)|D'Void]] by freezing his drilling machine.
*In a flashback in ''[[Special Delivery]]'', Big Chill defeated a DNAlien, but accidentally froze [[Ignacius Baumann|Mr. Baumann]]'s car at the same time.
*In '''''[[Ben 10: Alien Swarm]]''''', Big Chill battled a swarm of [[Microchip]]s.{{Refn|[[:File:Alien Swarm Chronology.png]]|group = DM}}
*In ''[[Vengeance of Vilgax: Part 2]]'', Big Chill was defeated by [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]], so he switched into [[Humungousaur (Classic)|Humungousaur]].
*In ''[[Inferno]]'', Big Chill captured [[Mouldywarp]].
*In ''[[Fool's Gold]]'', Big Chill battled [[Decka|primal Decka]] before switching into Echo Echo.
*In ''[[Singlehanded]]'', Big Chill, with no left hand, briefly fought some [[Vulpimancer (Classic)|Vulpimancers]] in the [[Null Void (Classic)|Null Void]] before switching into Swampfire.
*In ''[[Trade-Off!]]'', Big Chill defeated some [[Forever Knights]].
*In ''[[Above and Beyond]]'', Big Chill fought [[Alan Albright|Alan]], but was soon forced to retreat when the rest of the [[Plumbers' Helpers]] came to help Alan.
*In ''[[The Final Battle: Part 1]]'', Big Chill defeated [[Kraab (Classic)|Kraab]] before switching into Jetray to destroy some asteroids.

===Ultimate Alien===
*In ''[[Duped]]'', Big Chill was used by Film Fan Ben to fight [[Sir Urien]], but was defeated.
*In ''[[Hit 'Em Where They Live]]'', Big Chill battled some [[Pickaxe Alien]]s before going [[Ultimate Big Chill|Ultimate]]. Big Chill appeared again later when he was changing back to [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]].
*In ''[[Video Games (Episode)|Video Games]]'', Big Chill was scanned by [[Oliver Thompson]] for the [[Stalker]] off-screen. Later, he failed to defeat the Stalker, so he switched into [[Lodestar]].
*In ''[[Escape From Aggregor]]'', Big Chill fought [[Galapagus]] before going Ultimate. Big Chill appeared again later when he was changing back to [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]].
*In ''[[Too Hot to Handle]]'', Big Chill battled [[P'Andor]] before switching into [[Cannonbolt (Classic)|Cannonbolt]].
*In ''[[Ultimate Aggregor (Episode)|Ultimate Aggregor]]'', Big Chill went Ultimate to stop a group of fans from harassing him. Big Chill appeared again later when he was changing back to Ben.
*In ''[[Map of Infinity (Episode)|Map of Infinity]]'', Big Chill tried to negotiate with some white [[Necrofriggian (Classic)|Necrofriggian]] guards, but ended up having to fight them when he mentioned that he and [[Alien Force|the team]] had to "grab" an [[Map of Infinity|artifact]] from the [[Mikd'lty]] temple. Big Chill was then defeated by the guards, forcing him to switch into [[Echo Echo]].
*In ''[[Deep]]'', Big Chill chased [[Ultimate Aggregor]] before going Ultimate. Big Chill appeared again later when he was changing to [[Goop (Classic)|Goop]].
*In ''[[Absolute Power: Part 2]]'', Big Chill battled [[Ultimate Kevin]].
*In ''[[Viktor: The Spoils]]'', Big Chill snuck through a security grid, fought some Zarcovian soldiers and tried to keep [[Dr. Viktor]] frozen before going Ultimate. Big Chill appeared again later when he was changing back to Ben.
*In ''[[It's Not Easy Being Gwen]]'', Big Chill briefly battled [[Dr. Animo (Classic)|Dr. Animo]] and his [[Mutant Frog|mutant frog]].
*In ''[[Prisoner Number 775 is Missing]]'', Big Chill searched through an alien prison in [[Area 51]].
*In ''[[Greetings From Techadon]]'', Big Chill failed to get into the [[Techadon Factory]]. He then fought a silver [[Techadon Robot]] before going Ultimate.
*In ''[[The Flame Keepers' Circle]]'', Big Chill battled the [[Flame Keepers' Circle|Flame Keepers]] before going Ultimate. Big Chill appeared again later when he was changing back to Ben.
*In ''[[The Mother of All Vreedles]]'', Big Chill was defeated by [[Ma Vreedle]].
*In ''[[Ben 10-Generator Rex: Heroes United|Ben 10/Generator Rex: Heroes United]]'', Big Chill appeared thrice. Firstly, Big Chill escaped captivity and flew to what seemed like [[Bellwood (Classic)|Bellwood]], briefly freezing [[Rex Salazar (Generator Rex)|Rex]] along the way, before noticing that [[Mr. Smoothy (Classic)|Mr. Smoothy]] was replaced with [[Bob's Biscuit Barn]]. Later, he caught a falling Rex during their fight against [[Alpha]]. Lastly, he flew Rex onto a skyscraper to look over Alpha-Omega's rampage.
**Also, Big Chill appeared as one of the many aliens when [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was explaining his story to Rex.
*In ''[[The Eggman Cometh]]'', Big Chill defeated some [[Pterodactyl|pterodactyls]].
*In ''[[Night of the Living Nightmare]]'', [[Albedo|Negative]] Big Chill failed to defeat [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] before switching into Negative [[NRG]] in a dream.

===Omniverse===
*In ''[[Of Predators and Prey: Part 2]]'', Big Chill defeated [[Khyber]] before escaping the latter's [[Khyber's Ship|ship]] with [[Rook Blonko|Rook]].
*In ''[[Malefactor]]'', Big Chill fought [[Hypnotick]] before reverting back to avoid her hypnotism.
*In ''[[Showdown: Part 1]]'', Big Chill escaped [[Terroranchula (Transformation)|Terroranchula]]'s web and defeated [[Zed]], but was hypnotized by Hypnotick thrice.
*In ''[[Tummy Trouble]]'', Big Chill battled an [[Incursean (Classic)|Incursean]] in space. Later, Big Chill defeated another Incursean.
*In ''[[Ben Again]]'', Big Chill was used by 11-year-old [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] in 16-year-old Ben's body to find the [[Chrononavigator]].
*In ''[[The Frogs of War: Part 1]]'', Big Chill froze [[Milleous]].
*In ''[[The Ultimate Heist]]'', Big Chill appeared thrice. Firstly, Ben as Big Chill failed to break out of a [[Plumber Headquarters|Plumber HQ]] cell. Later, Ben as Big Chill escaped from [[Blukic]] and [[Driba]]. Lastly, [[Albedo|Negative]] Big Chill battled [[Thirteen]] before switching into Negative [[Wildvine (Classic)|Wildvine]].
*In ''[[Something Zombozo This Way Comes]]'', Big Chill froze some of the [[Zombie Clowns]] in place.
*In ''[[Let's Do the Time War Again]]'', Big Chill defeated [[Exo-Skull|Exo-Skull]] and [[Subdora]].
*In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', Big Chill appeared for a short time when Ben was cycling through his aliens.

