====[[Ben 10: Alien Force (Video Game)|Ben 10: Alien Force]]====
Big Chill is a playable alien in the Nintendo Wii, PlayStation 2, and PlayStation Portable versions of the game.

Big Chill and [[Swampfire]] are the only aliens available on [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]]'s arsenal at the beginning of the game.

Big Chill is able to glide across considerable distances, as well as ride on wind currents to temporarily increase his altitude.

Big Chill is used at the end of the Running on Autopilot level to survive the fall from the [[Highbreed Cruiser]].

Big Chill is vital for progression on The Forest Mid-evil/Medieval, Bombs Away!, A Few Bad Eggs, Plumber Trouble, Rural Rumble, and Running on Autopilot levels of the game.

====[[Ben 10 Alien Force: Vilgax Attacks]]====
Big Chill is a playable alien in the game.

=====Xbox 360, Nintendo Wii, PlayStation 2, and PlayStation Portable Versions=====
Due to the Omnitrix rebooting after Ben's abuse of the quick-change feature during his battle with an animated [[Mr. Smoothy (Classic)|Mr. Smoothy]] mascot, Big Chill, along with Swampfire, [[Spidermonkey (Classic)|Spidermonkey]], [[Humungousaur (Classic)|Humungousaur]], and [[Cannonbolt (Classic)|Cannonbolt]] were the only aliens available on Ben's arsenal upon his arrival on [[Vulpin]].

Like in ''[[Ben 10: Alien Force (Video Game)|Alien Force]]'', Big Chill is able to glide across considerable distances and ride on wind currents to temporarily increase his altitude.

Big Chill is capable of generating spiked balls of ice around his fists, as well as hurling ice spikes. He can also cause these spikes to sprout from the ground that surrounds him.

Big Chill is the only alien form capable of defeating [[Dr. Animo (Classic)|D'Void]], freezing the [[Kormite]] energy sources to weaken the otherwise invincible foe.

Ice Storm is an unlockable combo move for Big Chill.

Big Chill is vital for progression on the [[Bellwood (Classic)|Bellwood]], [[Terradino (Classic)|Terradino]], [[Encephalonus IV]], [[Anur Phaetos]], and [[Null Void (Classic)|Null Void]] levels of the game.

===== Nintendo DS Version=====
Big Chill and [[Brainstorm]] are reunlocked upon [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]]'s arrival on [[Encephalonus IV]].

Big Chill is able to glide across considerable distances and is the only alien capable of defeating [[Dr. Animo (Classic)|D'Void]].

Big Chill is vital for progression on the Encephalonus IV, [[MorOtesi]], and [[Null Void (Classic)|Null Void]] levels of the game.

====[[Ben 10 Alien Force: The Rise of Hex]]====
Big Chill is a playable alien in the game.

Due to the [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]] shorting out after [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] fiddled with it, Big Chill was temporarily locked until the beginning of Level 4.

Big Chill is able to double jump and glide across considerable distances, as well as slowly descend from a high altitude, avoiding hazards along the way.

====[[Ben 10 Ultimate Alien: Cosmic Destruction]]====
Big Chill is a playable alien in the game. Big Chill can be used for flight. His ice breath can be used to extinguish fire and freeze an object and enemies. He can attack with an "icy uppercut" as well as manipulate the cold around him to make a frosty tornado. His [[Ultimate Forms|Ultimate form]], [[Ultimate Big Chill]], is used in a boss battle.

Big Chill is vital for progression on The Great Wall and The Amazon levels of the game. He is also the default optional alien for The Final Battle level.

====[[Punch Time Explosion]] and [[Punch Time Explosion XL]]====
Big Chill is one of 16-year-old [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]]'s signature attacks in both games. Ben transforms into Big Chill, calling said name in form. He flies up into the air while dropping multiple ice shards which do 13% damage and creates three power cubes. He is one of Ben's strongest moves due to damage and range.

====[[Ben 10: Galactic Racing]]====
Big Chill is a playable racer in this game on all platforms.

====[[Ben 10: Omniverse 2]]====
Big Chill is a playable alien in the game.

===Online Games===
====[[Galactic Champions]]====
Big Chill, referred to as '''Necrofriggian''', is an alien found in the game. He is the final boss of the fifth tournament, the [[Mikd'lty]] Tournament.

Necrofriggian has above average Strength, average Agility, but lower Defense in comparison. His defensive options are quite strong, and he can inflict the Burn status effect, making him a reliable alien.

His offensive abilities are:
*Punch - Necrofriggian flies towards his opponent and punches them. Weak attack, doesn't waste any energy.
*Dash - Stronger variation of Punch, has a chance to lower enemy's Strength. Spends 13 energy.
*Sigh Ice - Necrofriggian uses his ice breath. Has a chance to lower enemy's Agility. Spends 24 energy.
*Ice Flames - Necrofriggian uses his ice breath. It's very likely to inflict the Burn effect on the enemy, and has a chance to also apply a Taunt effect and lower their Agility as well. Spends 35 energy.

His defensive abilities are:
*Block - Reduces damage taken this turn and recovers some energy.
*Impulse - Reduces damage taken this turn and increase attack stat. Spends 15 energy.
*Invisibility - Reduces damage taken this turn, cleanses status effects and increases Defense. Spends 24 energy.
*Ice Wall - Reduces damage taken this turn, heals self and increases Defense. Spends 35 energy.

====[[TKO]]====
Big Chill is a playable character in the game. His special moves are the Cold Rush and the Chill Out. His super move is the Ice Quake. His alternate color (when the players choose the same characters) is a darker blue/purple.

Big Chill is missing his wings, but [[Ultimate Big Chill]] still has his.

